  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to Coalition for Disaster Resilient Infrastructure</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(India):  .This activity supports the.Coalition for Disaster Resilient Infrastructure (CDRI). The United States.joined the Coalition as a founding member in December 2019. Led by India, the.CDRI is a partnership of national governments, U.N. agencies and programs,.multilateral development banks and financing mechanisms, the private sector,.and knowledge institutions. The Coalition aims to promote the resilience of new.and existing infrastructure systems to mitigate climate and disaster risks in.support of sustainable development. USAID will bolster India&apos;s leadership role.in disaster response and risk reduction and lead the South Asia region and.other member countries in addressing disaster risks by building the resilience.of communities and infrastructure..The objective of the activity is.to build technical capacities of the CDRI by improving the overall management.of the CDRI Secretariat by integrating key subject matter experts into the CDRI.Secretariat, provide targeted technical assistance, improve communications, and.enhance knowledge management. The activity supports the following Sustainable.Development Goals (SDGs): SDG 9 (Industry, Innovation, and Infrastructure) SDG.11 (Sustainable cities and communities and SDG 17 (Partnerships to achieve the.goals).  .FY 2022 funding will support five.key experts embedded in the CDRI Secretariat and support to strengthen the.institutional management and technical capacity of the CDRI. It will also be.used for training and capacity building, knowledge management, research, advocacy,.and partnerships activities, which will improve the service offerings of the.CDRI to advance infrastructure resilience in member countries.  Funds will.help develop and implement CDRI strategic communication plans as well as.generate content and support knowledge platforms...</narrative>
  </description>
